-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDERS 30 AND 31: REFERENCES UNDER ARTICLE 100 OF THE CONSTITUTION FOR ADVISORY OPINION; CONSTITUTIONAL CASE.  LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- Written with a macro builder that quotes the source lines and writes the @ref; the builder is not part of this row, so edit this file directly.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if" or "where" condition unmet.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a power or a duty limited by its own wording, a silence.
-- Most provisions of these two Orders address the Tribunal, a Judge, the Registrar or the Attorney-General.  They are encoded
-- for what they decide; the seat carries only what they mean to a person interested in the Reference or a party to the
-- proceedings in which a Case arose.  A period is timed by the helper of Order 28 (`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the act is done by the last day`).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 30 -- References under Article 100 of the Constitution for advisory opinion`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- application and definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4483 | 1. —(1) This Order applies, so far as applicable, to a Reference under Article 100 of the Constitution to a tribunal consisting of not less than 3 Supreme Court Judges for an opinion on a question as to the effect of any provision of the Constitution. (2) In this Order — “Reference” means a reference to the Tribunal made by the President of Singapore under Article 100 of the Constitution;
@ref O 30 r 1(1) (src:4483)
GIVEN `it is a Reference under Article 100 of the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to a tribunal consisting of not less than 3 Supreme Court Judges` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for an opinion on a question as to the effect of any provision of the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 30 r 1(1) this Order applies to the Reference` MEANS
    IF `it is a Reference under Article 100 of the Constitution` AND `it is to a tribunal consisting of not less than 3 Supreme Court Judges` AND `it is for an opinion on a question as to the effect of any provision of the Constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Order applies, so far as applicable, to a Reference under Article 100 of the Constitution to a tribunal consisting of not less than 3 Supreme Court Judges for an opinion on a question as to the effect of any provision of the Constitution"
