-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- reference by a State Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 1(1): "Despite Order 1, Rule 2, this Order applies where ...".  The words "Despite Order 1, Rule 2" switch off
-- O 1 r 2(8) for the proceedings within this Order (a seam of kind S-L2): the keel's function answers its own question, and
-- this one says that this Order applies to criminal proceedings in a State Court that raise a constitutional question.
-- src:4525 | 1. —(1) Despite Order 1, Rule 2, this Order applies where, in any proceedings including criminal proceedings in a State Court, a question arises as to the interpretation or effect of any provision of the Constitution, and the Court has pursuant to section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code stayed the proceedings, and the Court has stated the question in the form of a Case. (2) Every Case stated under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code must be divided into paragraphs and must concisely state such facts, must include such documents as may be necessary to enable the General Division to decide the question raised thereby, and must be signed by the District Judge, Magistrate, Coroner or Registrar, as the case may be.
