    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "The State Court must determine all questions and make all necessary orders regarding costs in the proceedings" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)

-- r 4(2): "no order for costs incurred in the General Division is to be made": a flat negative.
-- src:4536 | 4. —(1) Where the General Division has given judgment on the Case and the proceedings in the State Court in which the Case arose are still pending, the State Court is to continue such proceedings and dispose of the proceedings according to law. (2) The State Court must determine all questions and make all necessary orders regarding costs in the proceedings but no order for costs incurred in the General Division is to be made.
@ref O 31 r 4(2) no order (src:4536)
GIVEN `the State Court is making orders regarding costs in the proceedings in which the Case arose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 31 r 4(2) an order for costs incurred in the General Division may be made` MEANS
    IF `the State Court is making orders regarding costs in the proceedings in which the Case arose`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no order for costs incurred in the General Division is to be made"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): rule 4(2) speaks only of the State Court's orders on costs in the proceedings
